			<m_pNoteText type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1036{\fonttbl{\f0\froman\fprq10\fcharset0 Tahoma;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs16 When creating a flow, it is contained in the source element (system or function). If the source element is read only, then the flow is created in the target element (system or function). If the target element is read only, then the flow is created in the first writable package in the owner tree.\par%0D
During operational analysis, the SOI is always writable, during logical analysis, the user can creates flows between read only logical components, during technical analysis, the user can creates flows between technical components. It is also possible to creates flows in interface management packages between read only systems.\par%0D
\par%0D
\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</m_pNoteText>
		</CGIAnnotation>
